# iClass / Picopass default AUTHENTICATION keys (Kd / Kc), one 8-byte key per line (hex).
#
# These are GENUINELY PUBLIC keys: published in the academic work on iCLASS
# (Garcia et al., "Dismantling iCLASS", 2012; the loclass demo vectors) and in
# the PicoPass 2K documentation, and shipped openly in the Proxmark3 /
# RfidResearchGroup tree (client/dictionaries/iclass_default_keys.dic) from which
# this list is mirrored.  They are card-auth keys for the raw-frame / loclass
# path (hash0/elite diversification happens on top of these).
#
# NOT included here (by design, matching pm3 and RFIDIOt's "never commit real
# site/HID keys" rule): the leaked HID iCLASS 3DES *credential-decryption*
# (transport) key used by `iclass.py DECRYPT` - supply that yourself via
# -k / $RFIDIOT_ICLASS_DECRYPTKEY / ~/.rfidiot/iclass_decryptionkey.bin - and the
# large collected "elite" key dictionary (available in pm3 if you need it).

AEA684A6DAB23278  # AA1 - the well-known default iCLASS Kd (debit)
7665544332211000  # Kc from PicoPass 2K documentation
0123456789ABCDEF  # SAGEM
5B7C62C491C11B39  # loclass demo file
F0E1D2C3B4A59687  # Kd from PicoPass 2K documentation
5CBCF1DA45D5FB4F  # PicoPass default exchange key
31AD7EBD2F282168  # HID multiCLASS SE reader
6EFD46EFCBB3C875
E033CA419AEE43F9
2020666666668888  # iCL tags
6666202066668888  # iCS tags (reversed)
FDCB5A52EA8F3090
237FF9079863DF44
